@cc [owner:pmilliotte,label:architecture] resource-methods-take-caller-transaction
Resource methods that read or write FDB MUST take the caller's `&Transaction` and MUST NOT call
transaction runners or open a transaction themselves, so a caller can combine several resource
calls in one atomic transaction.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture;error-handling] cross-resource-error-propagation
Fallible resource methods MUST use their own concrete `Error` type, directly or through
`storage::Error<Error>`, rather than a caller-selected error type. Propagated domain errors from
another resource MUST appear as explicit typed variants, such as
`session::Error::Tenant(tenant::Error)`. Cross-resource `From` conversions MUST support `?`, wrapping
only `storage::Error::Resource` and preserving all other variants, including FDB failures, unchanged.
API translation MUST delegate wrapped domain errors to the originating resource's status mapping.

@cc [owner:id13,label:backend;concurrency] lock-expiry-index-atomicity
Each lock MUST have exactly one expiry index entry with the same tenant, object, and expiry.
Expiry index entries MUST NOT outlive their locks.
Acquisition, refresh, unlock, removal, and invalidation MUST update the lock and its index atomically.
Cleanup MUST read the expiry range with conflict tracking and clear each indexed lock and its index
entry in the same transaction, so concurrent renewal and cleanup cannot both commit.

@cc [owner:id13,label:security] lock-token-unpredictability
Each acquired lock token MUST have 74 independently cryptographically random UUIDv7 payload bits.
Lock tokens MUST NOT share an ordering counter with object IDs or other lock tokens.
